  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Village Capital Empowering Sustainable Entrepreneurship in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The initiative intends to strengthen the capacity of Entrepreneur Support Organisations (ESOs) and high-growth potential climate-focused startups in Ghana, Kenya, Malawi, Mozambique, and Tanzania. The initiative will take a dual-track approach: 1) equip impactful, community-led ESOs with the resources and experience needed to drive systems change, social and economic resiliency, and sustainable growth of national entrepreneurial ecosystems; and 2) accelerate and cultivate a long-term pipeline of high-growth, investible startups building solutions to enhance economic growth and resiliency in the blue economy, climate adaptation, food security, and renewabla energy sectors. 

The initiative will be divided into five separate components: i) landscape analysis and initative design, ii) ESO capacity building and support, iii) co-led direct entrepreneur support programs, iv) extended entrepreneur support, synthesis, and dissemination of data and learnings, and v) catalysing amd mobilizing capital. 
The program works to increase gender equity through direct work with entrepreneurs, ESOs, and their broader networks. They will use their in-house developed tools to increase gender equality, namely the Peer-Selection Framework and the Smarter Systems Toolkit, to mitigate bias and unlock overlooked opportunities for women entrepreneurs. Their online product, Abaca, incorporates equity-enhancing frameworks and data analysis tools to better understand the impact of their work on women entrepreneurs.</narrative>
  </description>
